(6689975, 998328, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Gave you a 6 in voting for the concept, but the execution needs a little more to make it pop.  The lighting is quite good,looks like you bounced the flash off the ceiling, and black bgs eat light, so good choice. I see you shot fairly fast so I''m guessing handheld; surprised that at f8 you have such a shallow dof.  You may want to invest in a tripod, they are worth it for shots like this.<br/> <br/>For what it is, the composition is fine, but there just isn''t enough of the guitar to see...if not for the title and hint of strings, I never would have guessed that they were tuners.  <br/> <br/>Please keep on shooting and entering, that''s the only way to improve.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Gave you a 6 in voting for the concept, but the execution needs a little more to make it pop.  The lighting is quite good,looks like you bounced the flash off the ceiling, and black bgs eat light, so good choice. I see you shot fairly fast so I''m guessing handheld; surprised that at f8 you have such a shallow dof.  You may want to invest in a tripod, they are worth it for shots like this. For what it is, the composition is fine, but there just isn''t enough of the guitar to see...if not for the title and hint of strings, I never would have guessed that they were tuners.   Please keep on shooting and entering, that''s the only way to improve. Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-02-24 01:44:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6689995, 998608, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Like this shot a lot, but am siding with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=10785" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">EL-ROI</a> and have to admit that it''s a) it''s gorgeous and b) it''s a shoehorn. And I'';m aggravated for you that most voters didn''t see what you were getting at, the rhythms in the lines and sinuous curves and funny little notes in between. <br/> <br/>As you yourself say, ''either way I shall enjoy the trip.'' Your work is very good, you have a marvelous eye and really seem to have a knack for b/w in particular.  And when you do ribbon - because I really do believe you could, if you stick with it and just keep on there is nothing better than ribboning on your terms, as opposed to selling out for the vox populi.<br/> <br/>Please keep on shooting and entering!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Like this shot a lot, but am siding with  EL-ROI and have to admit that it''s a) it''s gorgeous and b) it''s a shoehorn. And I'';m aggravated for you that most voters didn''t see what you were getting at, the rhythms in the lines and sinuous curves and funny little notes in between.  As you yourself say, ''either way I shall enjoy the trip.'' Your work is very good, you have a marvelous eye and really seem to have a knack for b/w in particular.  And when you do ribbon - because I really do believe you could, if you stick with it and just keep on there is nothing better than ribboning on your terms, as opposed to selling out for the vox populi. Please keep on shooting and entering! Feel free to PM me, Susan Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-02-24 01:53:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6690007, 998602, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First off congrats on a top 20 image, that''s nothing to sneeze at.  I''m glad to see a licorice pizza in the challenge and what looks like a fairly modern turntable - you don''t have a nickel taped to the head to keep it from skipping :-)<br/> <br/>OK now for the nitpicky part. A few hot areas on the arm and in the bg...hmm...and that''s really all I''ve got! The lighting is fine for this kind of shot, the composition is simple and clean, the dof is bang on and I find lots of atmosphere with the very light sepia tones.<br/> <br/>Overall good job, please keep on shooting and entering.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First off congrats on a top 20 image, that''s nothing to sneeze at.  I''m glad to see a licorice pizza in the challenge and what looks like a fairly modern turntable - you don''t have a nickel taped to the head to keep it from skipping :-) OK now for the nitpicky part. A few hot areas on the arm and in the bg...hmm...and that''s really all I''ve got! The lighting is fine for this kind of shot, the composition is simple and clean, the dof is bang on and I find lots of atmosphere with the very light sepia tones. Overall good job, please keep on shooting and entering. Feel free to PM me, Susan', '2012-02-24 02:00:44.000000', NULL, 0),
